From 000000000000000000000000000000000000000107 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: f <f@f>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: Skip interframe power collapse on the vpu20_4v firmware

With interframe power collapse enabled, the vpu20_4v firmware dies in
the VPP power-collapse handshake while encoding the very first frame
(the firmware log ends at "VppDec: PC refcount 0 and on is_needed 1");
the next register access resets the SoC. Observed on the Xiaomi 12T
Pro (SM8475) with every encoder session.

Skip the HFI property for the Gen2 firmware of VPU 2.0 only; the core
stays powered between frames. The SM8550 firmware data is unchanged.

Local Diting bring-up change, not submitted upstream.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
index d519dc0..8e7a845 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
@@ -1149,4 +1149,5 @@ const struct iris_firmware_data iris_hfi_gen2_vpu2_data = {
 	.dec_ip_int_buf_tbl = sm8450_dec_ip_int_buf_tbl,
 	.dec_ip_int_buf_tbl_size = ARRAY_SIZE(sm8450_dec_ip_int_buf_tbl),
 	.resume_without_payload = true,
+	.skip_interframe_pc = true,
 };
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
index 31427db..ac06897 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -59,6 +59,10 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_sys_interframe_powercollapse(struct iris_core *core)
 	struct iris_hfi_header *hdr;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* vpu20_4v: the firmware VPP dies at the first encoded frame */
+	if (core->iris_firmware_data->skip_interframe_pc)
+		return 0;
+
 	hdr = kzalloc(SYS_IFPC_PKT_SIZE, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!hdr)
 		return -ENOMEM;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_common.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_common.h
index 83ee9fc..ec55c8a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_common.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_platform_common.h
@@ -286,6 +286,7 @@ struct iris_firmware_data {
 
 	/* HFI_CMD_RESUME without payload (Gen2 firmware of VPU 2.0 SoCs) */
 	bool resume_without_payload;
+	bool skip_interframe_pc;
 };
 
 struct iris_firmware_desc {
